.TH smi-encrypt "1" "June 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Encryption Command"
.SH NAME
smi-encrypt \- Encrypt a file using AES-256-CBC with HMAC-SHA-512 integrity protection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-encrypt
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-encrypt
encrypts the specified
.I FILE
using OpenSSL with AES-256-CBC symmetric encryption.
The passphrase is read interactively from the terminal without echo; it must be entered twice for confirmation.
The encrypted output is written to
.IR FILE .enc .
An HMAC-SHA-512 integrity tag is written to
.IR FILE .enc.hmac .
Upon successful encryption the original file is removed.
.PP
Key derivation uses PBKDF2 with HMAC-SHA-256 and 600\,000 iterations (NIST SP\ 800-132 / OWASP\ 2023
recommended minimum), with a random salt stored in the encrypted file header.
.PP
The command is suitable for encrypting both
.B text and binary files
of any size.
AES-256-CBC operates as a chained block cipher over the data, so there is
.B no upper limit on file size
imposed by the key or block size.
Large archives, database dumps, ISO images, and other binary data can all be encrypted with this command.
.PP
The passphrase is entered via the terminal (stdin) without any graphical or TUI pinentry dialog,
making the command safe to use over SSH and in non-graphical environments.
.PP
.B Note:
files encrypted with earlier versions of this tool (10\,000 iterations, no HMAC file) are not
compatible with the current version and must be decrypted with the matching older version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I FILE
Path to the plain-text or binary file to encrypt.
Must be an existing regular file.
The file is removed after successful encryption.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
File encrypted successfully; original file removed.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid usage: wrong number of arguments, file does not exist, or passphrases do not match.
.TP
.B 2
Encryption or HMAC generation failed; no files are removed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Encrypt a configuration file:
.IP
smi-encrypt secrets.conf
.PP
Two files are produced:
.IR secrets.conf.enc
(ciphertext) and
.IR secrets.conf.enc.hmac
(integrity tag).
Decrypt with:
.IP
smi-decrypt secrets.conf.enc
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
